# Force LF line endings on checkout for every text file, regardless of the
# checking-out machine's own git config (core.autocrlf) or OS. Without this,
# a Windows checkout with the very common core.autocrlf=true default
# rewrites every text file - including every deploy/*.sh script and .env* -
# to CRLF. Two concrete, confirmed failure modes that causes:
#   1. Every bash script under deploy/ and scripts/ fails outright - either
#      "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M: no such file or directory" (CRLF in
#      the shebang line) when run directly, or `$'\r': command not found`
#      part-way through, depending on how it's invoked.
#   2. deploy/lib/kx_license.sh's own `grep ... .env | cut -d= -f2-` value
#      extraction (and any script that does the same) picks up a trailing
#      \r on every value if the user's OWN .env also has CRLF - so
#      `[ "$env_source" = "kx-portal" ]` silently evaluates false even on a
#      correctly-configured .env, surfacing as "Missing KDB-X binary/
#      license" with no obvious connection to line endings at all.
# `eol=lf` normalizes the WORKING TREE to LF on checkout; it does not touch
# the repo's stored blobs. A checkout that already happened before this file
# existed needs a fresh `git add --renormalize .` (or a re-clone) to apply -
# see docs/troubleshooting.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh eol=lf
*.q eol=lf
*.py eol=lf
*.js eol=lf
*.jsx eol=lf
*.env eol=lf
.env.example eol=lf
Dockerfile* eol=lf
*.yml eol=lf
*.yaml eol=lf

# Known binaries - never touched by text normalization, but explicit here so
# a future `* text=auto` tweak can't accidentally start mangling them.
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
